C('Combining numeric types','x = 4 + 0.5\nprint(x, type(x).__name__)','4.5 float',['4 int','4.5 int','45 str'],'Adding an int and a float produces a float here.')
C('Text repetition','print("ha" * 3)','hahaha',['haha','ha3','9'],'String multiplication repeats the text the requested number of times.')
C('A formatted length','length = 1.23456\nprint(f"{length:.3f} m")','1.235 m',['1.234 m','1.23 m','1.23456 m'],'The format displays three digits after the decimal point, with rounding.')
C('Separating printed fields','print("P", 12, sep=":", end="!\\n")','P:12!',['P 12!','P:12','P12!'],'sep inserts a colon between the two fields, and end supplies the exclamation mark and newline.')
C('Text addition versus arithmetic','print("12" + "3", 12 + 3)','123 15',['15 15','123 123','36 15'],'+ concatenates strings but adds numeric operands.')
C('A conversion before multiplication','raw = "2.5"\nprint(float(raw) * 4)','10.0',['2.52.52.52.5','10','6.5'],'Converting the text to float makes multiplication numerical.')
C('Kilometres to metres','distance_km = 1.75\nprint(distance_km * 1000)','1750.0',['1.75','0.00175','175.0'],'There are 1000 metres in a kilometre, so the numeric length increases by that factor.')
C('Minutes to seconds','minutes = 7\nprint(minutes * 60)','420',['7','0.11666666666666667','67'],'The conversion multiplies by sixty seconds per minute.')
C('A stress calculation','force_n = 90\narea_m2 = 0.003\nprint(force_n / area_m2)','30000.0',['0.000033333333333333335','270.0','30.0'],'Stress in pascals is force in newtons divided by area in square metres.')
C('An efficiency fraction','input_w = 120\nefficiency = 0.75\nprint(input_w * efficiency)','90.0',['160.0','9000.0','119.25'],'A 75 percent conversion retains 0.75 of the input under this illustrative model.')
C('A percentage increase','initial = 80\nfinal = initial * 1.25\nprint(final)','100.0',['20.0','81.25','64.0'],'A 25 percent increase multiplies the original by 1.25.')
C('A negative floor quotient','print(-9 // 4, -9 % 4)','-3 3',['-2 -1','-2 3','-3 -1'],'The quotient rounds down to -3, and -9 equals 4*(-3)+3.')
C('Comparison produces a Boolean','limit = 40\nprint(40 <= limit, type(40 <= limit).__name__)','True bool',['40 int','False bool','True int'],'The inclusive comparison succeeds and has Boolean type.')
C('Converting Boolean values','print(int(True), int(False))','1 0',['True False','0 1','1 1'],'The two Boolean values convert to one and zero respectively.')
C('A simultaneous swap','a, b = 3, 8\na, b = b, a\nprint(a, b)','8 3',['8 8','3 3','3 8'],'Both right-side values are evaluated before the two target bindings change.')
C('An augmented update','energy = 10\nenergy *= 3\nenergy -= 4\nprint(energy)','26',['18','6','30'],'The updates first produce 30, then subtract four.')
C('Reassigning a new type','reading = 5\nreading = str(reading)\nprint(type(reading).__name__, reading + "0")','str 50',['int 5','str 5','int 50'],'str returns text, so the later + concatenates the two strings.')
C('An explicit newline','print("top\\nbottom")','top\nbottom',['top bottom','top\\nbottom','topbottom'],'The newline escape inside the string starts a second printed line.')
C('Mass conversion before weight','mass_g = 500\nprint(mass_g / 1000 * 9.8)','4.9',['4900.0','49.0','0.49'],'Converting 500 grams to 0.5 kilograms gives a weight of 4.9 newtons in this model.')
C('An absolute difference','print(abs(12 - 19))','7',['-7','31','1.5833333333333333'],'abs returns the nonnegative magnitude of the difference.')
C('Two representations of zero','print(bool(0), bool(0.01))','False True',['False False','True True','True False'],'Numeric zero is false; a nonzero numeric value is true in this Boolean conversion.')
C('Rounding only for display','x = 2 / 3\nprint(f"{x:.2f}", x > 0.66)','0.67 True',['0.66 True','0.67 False','0.66 False'],'Formatting rounds the displayed value while the underlying x remains greater than 0.66.')
C('Power and unary minus','print(-2**2, (-2)**2)','-4 4',['4 4','-4 -4','4 -4'],'Exponentiation binds before the leading minus unless parentheses include the negative base.')
C('A named constant in a formula','gravity = 10\nmass = 6\nheight = 3\nprint(mass * gravity * height)','180',['19','60','18'],'The illustrative potential-energy formula multiplies all three input quantities.')
C('Quoting a numeric label','label = "3.0"\nprint(len(label), type(label).__name__)','3 str',['3 float','1 str','3.0 float'],'The string contains three characters, including its decimal point.')
C('A copied scalar value','a = 2.0\nb = a\na += 0.5\nprint(a, b)','2.5 2.0',['2.5 2.5','2.0 2.5','2.0 2.0'],'Updating a binds its new float value without changing b.')
T('Which variable name is valid Python?', 'flow_rate',['2flow','flow-rate','for'],'Names may use letters, digits and underscores, but cannot begin with a digit or use a reserved keyword.')
T('Which expression gives energy in joules from power_w and time_s?', 'power_w * time_s',['power_w / time_s','time_s / power_w','power_w + time_s'],'A watt is a joule per second; multiplying by seconds yields joules.')
T('What does the assignment x = y establish?', 'x is bound to the value referenced by y',['y is always copied recursively','x and y must remain equal forever','Python solves an equation for y'],'Assignment binds a name; later rebinding and mutable-object behavior must be considered separately.')
T('Which expression converts decimal-point text raw to a number?', 'float(raw)',['str(raw)','len(raw)','type(raw)'],'float parses supported numeric text; the other operations do not perform this numeric conversion.')
T('Which is a floating-point literal?', '4.0',['"4.0"','4','"4"'],'A decimal point in this unquoted literal gives a float, while quotes create text.')
T('Why put units in names such as distance_m?', 'To make dimensional meaning visible',['To make Python enforce the unit automatically','To prevent all numeric rounding','To require that every value be positive'],'The name documents intended units, helping review, but does not impose a runtime unit type.')
T('Which operator represents exponentiation in Python?', '**',['^','//','%'],'** raises a base to a power; ^ is a different bitwise operation for integers.')
T('Which comparison includes equality at the upper limit?', 'value <= limit',['value < limit','value > limit','value != limit'],'The <= relation permits a value exactly equal to its limit.')
T('What does a comment beginning with # usually do?', 'Documents code without being executed as a statement',['Prints the remaining text','Creates a string variable automatically','Runs only in a loop'],'A comment explains intent or context; it is ignored during ordinary execution.')
T('Which conversion is appropriate for seconds from hours?', 'hours * 3600',['hours / 3600','hours * 60','hours + 3600'],'One hour contains sixty minutes of sixty seconds, giving a factor of 3600.')
T('A meaningful engineering output should normally include:', 'The quantity and its unit alongside the result',['Only the variable memory address','Only a bare rounded number in every context','A claim that code execution validates the physical model'],'The label and unit make the number interpretable under the stated model.')
T('Which is the best reason to state an input assumption?', 'It defines the domain in which the calculation is intended to apply',['It proves all possible inputs valid','It makes every exception disappear','It changes the numeric value automatically'],'Assumptions delimit the contract and support meaningful tests and interpretation.')
T('What distinguishes a syntax error from a wrong engineering formula?', 'A syntax error violates Python grammar; a wrong formula may still execute',['Both always stop parsing','A wrong formula is always a SyntaxError','Python checks the physical meaning of every expression'],'Grammar checks do not establish that a valid expression models the intended relationship.')
T('Which expression correctly scales a length from metres to millimetres?', 'length_m * 1000',['length_m / 1000','length_m * 100','length_m / 100'],'The numerical length in millimetres is one thousand times the numerical length in metres.')
