C('A logical interval','x = 7\nprint(3 <= x < 7)','False',['True','7','3'],'The upper inequality is strict, so seven itself is excluded.')
T('Which choice prevents an alternative branch after the first successful classification?', 'An if/elif/else chain',['Several independent if statements','An unconditional print after every branch','A loop with no condition'],'The chain chooses one branch at most; independent if statements can all run.')
T('Which statement ends the nearest loop immediately?', 'break',['continue','pass','else'],'break exits the loop, whereas continue advances to its next iteration and pass does nothing.')
T('Which statement skips the remaining body of one loop iteration?', 'continue',['break','return in every context','pass'],'continue resumes with the loop’s next iteration rather than ending the entire loop.')
T('Why initialize a sum before a loop?', 'The accumulator needs a defined starting value',['It makes all inputs positive','It forces the loop to run once','It removes the need to update the total'],'Starting at zero provides the additive identity and avoids using an unbound name.')
T('Which input checks the boundary of x < 50 most directly?', '50',['20','80','-10'],'The equality value distinguishes a strict comparison from one that includes its endpoint.')
T('How many values does range(4) produce?', '4',['3','5','0'],'It produces zero, one, two and three: four values in total.')
T('Which Boolean expression requires both tests?', 'a and b',['a or b','not a','a != b in every case'],'Conjunction is true only when both Boolean tests are true.')
T('A while loop’s termination argument should identify:', 'A state change that eventually makes its condition false',['Only the loop’s indentation','Only a print statement','A variable that never changes'],'Reasoning about progress prevents repeating the same condition and state indefinitely.')
T('Which initializer is appropriate for a product of factors?', '1',['0','None','An empty string'],'One is the multiplicative identity; starting at zero would erase every finite numeric factor.')
T('Which indentation describes a statement inside a loop body?', 'It is indented consistently under the loop header',['It must begin in the same column as the header','It must have exactly one space in every program','It must be on the line before the header'],'Python uses consistent block indentation to determine which statements belong to the loop.')
