C('A simple returned product','def triple(x):\n    return x*3\nprint(triple(7))','21',['10','7','None'],'The parameter receives seven and the return expression multiplies it by three.')
C('A default scale factor','def scale(x, factor=2):\n    return x*factor\nprint(scale(5), scale(5, 3))','10 15',['10 10','5 15','15 10'],'The first call uses the default; the second supplies a replacement factor.')
C('Keyword argument order','def difference(a, b):\n    return a-b\nprint(difference(b=2, a=9))','7',['-7','11','2'],'Keyword names, rather than their written order, bind a to nine and b to two.')
C('The implicit None result','def announce(x):\n    print(x)\nresult = announce(4)\nprint(result)','4\nNone',['4','None','4\n4'],'The call prints four but reaches its end without returning a value, so result is None.')
C('Return ends one call','def choose(x):\n    return x+1\n    print("later")\nprint(choose(2))','3',['later\n3','3\nlater','None'],'Execution of the function call stops at return; the later print is unreachable.')
C('A local name masks a global','x = 8\ndef f():\n    x = 3\n    return x\nprint(f(), x)','3 8',['3 3','8 8','8 3'],'The function’s assignment creates a local x and leaves the outer binding unchanged.')
C('Reading an enclosing value','offset = 5\ndef add_offset(x):\n    return x+offset\nprint(add_offset(2))','7',['2','5','NameError'],'The function can read the module-level offset when it has no local binding of that name.')
C('Independent repeated calls','def f(x):\n    x += 2\n    return x\nprint(f(1), f(1))','3 3',['3 5','1 1','None None'],'Each call begins with its own parameter binding of one.')
C('An unchanged caller scalar','def increase(x):\n    x += 10\na = 2\nincrease(a)\nprint(a)','2',['12','None','10'],'Rebinding the local integer parameter does not rebind the caller’s a.')
C('An explicitly returned update','def increase(x):\n    return x+10\na = 2\na = increase(a)\nprint(a)','12',['2','10','None'],'The caller assigns the returned value to its own variable.')
C('A returned pair','def bounds(xs):\n    return min(xs), max(xs)\nprint(bounds([4, 1, 7]))','(1, 7)',['[1, 7]','1 7','(4, 7)'],'The comma-separated return creates a tuple containing the two extrema.')
C('Unpacking returned values','def parts(n):\n    return n//3, n%3\nq, r = parts(11)\nprint(q, r)','3 2',['2 3','3 3','11 3'],'The returned quotient and remainder bind to q and r in order.')
C('A Boolean query function','def within(x):\n    return 0 <= x <= 5\nprint(within(0), within(6))','True False',['False False','True True','False True'],'The inclusive lower endpoint passes, while six exceeds the upper bound.')
C('A conditional early return','def safe_ratio(a, b):\n    if b == 0:\n        return None\n    return a/b\nprint(safe_ratio(6, 0), safe_ratio(6, 3))','None 2.0',['0 2','None 2','ZeroDivisionError'],'The first call exits before division; the second computes a float quotient.')
C('A helper called twice','def square(x):\n    return x*x\nprint(square(2)+square(3))','13',['25','10','6'],'The two calls independently return four and nine.')
C('Composing two functions','def double(x):\n    return 2*x\ndef shift(x):\n    return x+3\nprint(double(shift(4)))','14',['11','10','7'],'The inner call returns seven, which becomes the outer call’s input.')
C('Order of composition matters','def double(x):\n    return 2*x\ndef shift(x):\n    return x+3\nprint(shift(double(4)))','11',['14','10','7'],'The inner doubling gives eight before the outer shift adds three.')
C('Tracing calls and returns','def f(x):\n    print("inside", x)\n    return x+1\nprint("outside", f(2))','inside 2\noutside 3',['outside 3\ninside 2','inside 3\noutside 2','outside 2'],'The argument expression f(2) completes before the outer print can display its fields.')
C('Returning a new list','def doubled(xs):\n    return [2*x for x in xs]\na = [1, 3]\nprint(doubled(a), a)','[2, 6] [1, 3]',['[2, 6] [2, 6]','None [2, 6]','[1, 3] [1, 3]'],'The comprehension constructs a new list and leaves the caller’s input unchanged.')
C('Mutating a list parameter','def add_last(xs):\n    xs.append(8)\na = [2]\nadd_last(a)\nprint(a)','[2, 8]',['[2]','[8]','None'],'The parameter references the same mutable list as the caller’s a.')
C('Rebinding a list parameter','def replace(xs):\n    xs = [8]\na = [2]\nreplace(a)\nprint(a)','[2]',['[8]','[2, 8]','None'],'Rebinding xs changes only the local name, not the caller’s binding.')
C('A sum computed inside a function','def total(xs):\n    result = 0\n    for x in xs:\n        result += x\n    return result\nprint(total([2, -1, 4]))','5',['7','4','0'],'The local accumulator adds each value before being returned.')
C('A fresh accumulator per call','def total(xs):\n    result = 0\n    for x in xs:\n        result += x\n    return result\nprint(total([1, 2]), total([4]))','3 4',['3 7','0 0','None None'],'Initialization occurs separately each time the function is called.')
C('A small unit conversion helper','def minutes(seconds):\n    return seconds/60\nprint(minutes(90))','1.5',['5400','1','30'],'The helper converts seconds to minutes by division by sixty.')
C('An identity case in a formula','def energy(mass, speed):\n    return 0.5*mass*speed**2\nprint(energy(4, 0))','0.0',['2.0','4','None'],'A zero speed makes the squared-speed factor zero.')
C('A keyword overriding one default','def report(value, unit="Pa", digits=1):\n    return f"{value:.{digits}f} {unit}"\nprint(report(12.345, digits=2))','12.35 Pa',['12.3 Pa','12.35 2','12.345 Pa'],'The named digits argument changes only precision; unit retains its default.')
C('A function supplied as an argument','def apply(function, x):\n    return function(x)\ndef square(x):\n    return x*x\nprint(apply(square, 5))','25',['5','10','None'],'The function object square is passed without being called until apply uses it.')
C('A lambda conversion','convert = lambda x: 2*x+1\nprint(convert(6))','13',['12','7','None'],'The lambda returns its single expression for x equal to six.')
C('A closure remembers a factor','def make_scale(factor):\n    def scale(x):\n        return factor*x\n    return scale\nby_three = make_scale(3)\nprint(by_three(4))','12',['7','3','NameError'],'The returned nested function retains access to its enclosing factor binding.')
C('Two independent closures','def make_add(offset):\n    return lambda x: x+offset\na = make_add(2)\nb = make_add(5)\nprint(a(3), b(3))','5 8',['8 8','5 5','2 5'],'The two factory calls establish different enclosing offsets.')
C('A shadowed parameter name','value = 10\ndef f(value):\n    return value-1\nprint(f(4), value)','3 10',['3 4','9 10','3 3'],'The parameter masks the module binding only during the call.')
C('A return with two branches','def sign(x):\n    if x < 0:\n        return -1\n    return 1\nprint(sign(-2), sign(0))','-1 1',['-1 0','1 1','-2 0'],'Under this function’s stated code, zero follows the nonnegative return path.')
C('A missing return on one path','def positive(x):\n    if x > 0:\n        return True\nprint(positive(-2))','None',['False','True','-2'],'The negative-input path reaches the end without a return statement.')
C('A definition is not a call','def f():\n    print("run")\nprint("ready")','ready',['run\nready','ready\nrun','No output'],'Defining f stores the function; its body runs only if f is called.')
C('A function object under another name','def increment(x):\n    return x+1\nother = increment\nprint(other(9))','10',['9','None','NameError'],'Assignment gives another name to the callable function object.')
C('Argument expressions run first','def add(a, b):\n    return a+b\nprint(add(2*3, 4+1))','11',['10','9','15'],'The argument expressions evaluate to six and five before binding the parameters.')
C('A mean with an explicit empty policy','def mean(xs):\n    return sum(xs)/len(xs) if xs else None\nprint(mean([]), mean([2, 6]))','None 4.0',['0 4','None 8','ZeroDivisionError'],'The conditional expression chooses None for the empty list and computes the nonempty mean.')
C('A helper used by a loop','def square(x):\n    return x*x\nprint([square(x) for x in range(4)])','[0, 1, 4, 9]',['[1, 4, 9, 16]','[0, 1, 2, 3]','[0, 2, 4, 6]'],'The helper is called with zero, one, two and three.')
C('A tuple argument remains one argument','def count_pair(pair):\n    return len(pair)\nprint(count_pair((4, 7)))','2',['11','4','TypeError'],'The parenthesized pair is one tuple object with two elements.')
C('Unpacking arguments with a star','def multiply(a, b):\n    return a*b\nvalues = (3, 5)\nprint(multiply(*values))','15',['8','(3, 5)','TypeError'],'The star expands the two tuple elements into the two positional arguments.')
C('A named intermediate value','def rectangle_perimeter(w, h):\n    half = w+h\n    return 2*half\nprint(rectangle_perimeter(3, 6))','18',['9','36','12'],'The intermediate sum is nine and the returned perimeter doubles it.')
C('An inner helper with a documented operation','def area_after_scale(w, h, scale):\n    def area(a, b):\n        return a*b\n    return area(w*scale, h*scale)\nprint(area_after_scale(2, 3, 2))','24',['12','6','48'],'Scaling both dimensions by two increases area by four.')
C('An explicitly global update','count = 0\ndef step():\n    global count\n    count += 1\nstep()\nstep()\nprint(count)','2',['0','1','None'],'The global declaration directs the assignments to the module-level count.')
C('A local calculation leaves external state','count = 5\ndef next_count(count):\n    return count+1\nnew = next_count(count)\nprint(count, new)','5 6',['6 6','5 5','6 5'],'The function returns a derived value without rebinding the external count.')
C('A returned string query','def label(sensor, value):\n    return sensor+":"+str(value)\nprint(label("S2", 8))','S2:8',['S2 8','S28','sensor:8'],'The function converts the integer to text before concatenating the label.')
C('Named numerator and denominator','def divide(numerator, denominator):\n    return numerator/denominator\nprint(divide(denominator=4, numerator=10))','2.5',['0.4','2','6'],'The names bind ten as numerator and four as denominator despite reversed written order.')
C('A function returning another call','def shift(x):\n    return x+2\ndef twice_shift(x):\n    return shift(shift(x))\nprint(twice_shift(1))','5',['3','6','4'],'The two nested calls add two successively: one becomes three, then five.')
C('An immutable string parameter','def lower_local(text):\n    text = text.lower()\n    return text\nraw = "ABC"\nprint(lower_local(raw), raw)','abc ABC',['abc abc','ABC ABC','ABC abc'],'The local transformed string is returned while the caller’s original binding remains unchanged.')
C('A default None creates fresh state','def record(value, history=None):\n    if history is None:\n        history = []\n    history.append(value)\n    return history\nprint(record(1), record(2))','[1] [2]',['[1, 2] [1, 2]','[1] [1, 2]','None None'],'Each omitted history argument takes the branch creating a new list.')
C('An explicitly supplied history is reused','def record(value, history):\n    history.append(value)\n    return len(history)\nvalues = [2]\nprint(record(4, values), values)','2 [2, 4]',['1 [2]','2 [4]','None [2, 4]'],'The append mutates the supplied list, then its new length is returned.')
T('A parameter is best described as:', 'A name in a function definition that receives an argument',['The printed result of every call','Only a global variable','A mandatory numeric literal'],'Parameters describe the function’s inputs; arguments are the supplied call-time expressions.')
T('Why write a function contract?', 'To state inputs, results, side effects and relevant assumptions',['To guarantee no tests are needed','To force every result to be numeric','To prevent function calls'],'A contract supports callers and gives tests an independent basis for expected behavior.')
T('What distinguishes print from return?', 'print displays a value; return delivers a value to the caller',['They are interchangeable in all functions','print always returns the displayed argument','return automatically displays a value in a script'],'A displayed result is not automatically available as the function’s return value.')
T('Which choice improves decomposition?', 'Separate operations with clear responsibilities and interfaces',['Duplicate the same formula in every caller','Use unrelated global state for every intermediate result','Put the whole project in one giant expression'],'A small operation can be reasoned about and tested independently of the complete workflow.')
T('When is a function body executed?', 'When that function is called',['Immediately every time its name is displayed','Only when the program ends','Every time any variable changes'],'Definition creates the function object; a call executes its body with argument bindings.')
T('What does a function return when it reaches the end without an explicit return?', 'None',['Its last local variable automatically','Zero in every case','True in every case'],'Python uses None as the implicit return value.')
T('Why is a mutable default list potentially surprising?', 'The same default object can be reused by later calls',['Python copies every default recursively','Lists cannot be parameters','The default is always discarded before a call'],'Default expressions are evaluated at definition time, so retained mutable state can span calls.')
T('Which is a function side effect?', 'Changing a list supplied by the caller',['Computing a new local integer only','Returning a new numeric result only','Reading a documented constant only'],'Mutation of externally observable state is a side effect that callers need to know about.')
T('Why pass a function as an argument?', 'To reuse a procedure with different specified operations',['To execute every function in the module','To eliminate parameter binding','To force recursion'],'Higher-order functions can separate a general procedure from the operation it applies.')
T('Which test checks a function that promises no input mutation?', 'Save an independent input copy and compare it after the call',['Create another name for the same list and assume it is a snapshot','Inspect only the function name','Skip checking the input'],'A genuine snapshot is necessary to detect whether the original contents changed.')
